# Worktree Management

- When creating an auxiliary git worktree for agent work, do not place it as a sibling inside the active multi-repo workspace parent. This can confuse other agents and repo discovery.
- Prefer a dedicated external parent such as `/Users/kevin.spears/code/worktrees/<repo>-<task>` unless the user requests a specific location.
- Keep the primary checkout in its original workspace path unless the user explicitly asks to move it.
- After a branch or MR is merged, clean up its auxiliary worktree with `git worktree remove <path>` once any needed changes are committed or intentionally discarded.
- After removing a worktree, run `git worktree list` from the primary repo to verify the stale worktree is gone.
